# Calculator rules

- Calculators are pure functions with typed inputs and outputs. No DOM access, no network calls, no hidden constants.
- Validate inputs: reject negative numbers, division by zero, margins of 100% or more. Return clear error messages, not NaN.
- Round only for display, not inside calculations. Use 2 decimals for money.
- Every calculator needs unit tests with hand-checked known answers (see docs/TASKS.md).
- Show the formula in plain English on the tool page, plus one worked example.
- Add a short limits note: "Estimates only. Not tax, legal or financial advice."
- Any fee, rate or threshold used by a calculator must come from data/, never hard-coded.
